1
00:00:12,738 --> 00:00:15,938
(Jung Yong Hwa)

2
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:19,038
(Hong Seung Hee)

3
00:00:19,108 --> 00:00:22,308
(Lee Yi Kyung)

4
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,278
(Park Yu Na)

5
00:00:36,628 --> 00:00:40,028
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:40,098 --> 00:00:41,528
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:41,598 --> 00:00:43,038
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:47,008 --> 00:00:49,508
It really was my father.

9
00:00:56,278 --> 00:00:59,348
Han Jung Woo, no, Um Tae Bong.

10
00:00:59,418 --> 00:01:03,258
Please, find my father.

11
00:01:05,388 --> 00:01:06,388
Let's go for now.

12
00:01:09,928 --> 00:01:11,558
(Episode 4)

13
00:01:12,558 --> 00:01:16,238
It was right here. He definitely went this way earlier.

14
00:01:16,298 --> 00:01:17,868
Does that make sense?

15
00:01:17,938 --> 00:01:20,008
You must have seen it wrong.

16
00:01:20,068 --> 00:01:22,008
No, it was definitely my father.

17
00:01:42,658 --> 00:01:43,728
I'm sorry.

18
00:01:57,478 --> 00:01:58,538
The person you saw earlier...

19
00:02:00,148 --> 00:02:02,078
What was he wearing? Tell me in detail.

20
00:02:06,018 --> 00:02:08,088
Don't look at me like that. You said you really saw him.

21
00:02:08,148 --> 00:02:09,388
If it really was your father,

22
00:02:12,618 --> 00:02:13,828
there must be a reason.

23
00:03:00,038 --> 00:03:01,168
Excuse me.

24
00:03:01,868 --> 00:03:02,878
I'm sorry.

25
00:03:10,718 --> 00:03:11,718
Sir?

26
00:03:22,028 --> 00:03:23,028
Did you find him?

27
00:03:28,298 --> 00:03:30,398
See? You were mistaken.

28
00:03:31,468 --> 00:03:33,838
- Your father is not here.
- Hey, it's Um Tae Bong.

29
00:03:33,908 --> 00:03:36,168
Oh, it really is Um Tae Bong. Who is the woman next to him?

30
00:03:36,168 --> 00:03:37,778
- Take it off.
- Is she his girlfriend?

31
00:03:37,778 --> 00:03:39,648
Take it off before your face gets exposed.

32
00:03:40,248 --> 00:03:42,878
- I think it is him.
- It is Um Tae Bong.

33
00:03:42,948 --> 00:03:44,778
It's Um Tae Bong. Right?

34
00:03:44,848 --> 00:03:46,388
- It is.
- You're right.

35
00:03:48,748 --> 00:03:49,758
An exclusive...

36
00:03:50,818 --> 00:03:53,858
Where did you learn such terrible manners,

37
00:03:54,158 --> 00:03:55,958
touching others and filming without permission?

38
00:03:58,628 --> 00:04:01,028
Was the line I said during yesterday's shoot,

39
00:04:01,098 --> 00:04:03,398
but it would be best if a line just remains a line, right?

40
00:04:03,468 --> 00:04:04,638
Oh, yes.

41
00:04:07,268 --> 00:04:08,268
Let's go.

42
00:04:11,308 --> 00:04:13,978
(Janchi Noodles, Bibim Noodles)

43
00:04:16,748 --> 00:04:17,918
You can go by yourself, right?

44
00:04:17,978 --> 00:04:18,978
Yes.

45
00:04:20,688 --> 00:04:21,718
Oh, hey.

46
00:04:23,488 --> 00:04:24,788
That line from earlier...

47
00:04:26,188 --> 00:04:27,688
was pretty cool.

48
00:04:29,998 --> 00:04:30,998
It wasn't a line.

49
00:04:33,828 --> 00:04:35,728
This woman is overestimating me.

50
00:04:35,798 --> 00:04:38,038
Do I look like someone who would remember a line after the shoot?

51
00:04:40,538 --> 00:04:41,538
Get going.

52
00:04:42,808 --> 00:04:45,478
Thank you, Um Tae Bong.

53
00:04:52,478 --> 00:04:53,488
What?

54
00:04:55,718 --> 00:04:57,718
I think you just said something.

55
00:05:03,158 --> 00:05:05,298
Don't get distracted and go straight home.

56
00:05:59,688 --> 00:06:00,688
What?

57
00:06:04,188 --> 00:06:05,188
Hong Du.

58
00:06:05,688 --> 00:06:07,728
Is something wrong?

59
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:10,758
Oh, this.

60
00:06:13,968 --> 00:06:17,138
My father is a bit shy,

61
00:06:17,538 --> 00:06:19,168
so we will have to postpone tonight's dinner invitation.

62
00:06:22,008 --> 00:06:23,438
Then next time,

63
00:06:23,908 --> 00:06:25,738
we will have something even more delicious than today's menu.

64
00:06:26,178 --> 00:06:27,178
Okay.

65
00:06:48,828 --> 00:06:50,098
Hey.

66
00:06:51,768 --> 00:06:52,768
I'm sorry.

67
00:06:55,408 --> 00:06:56,878
I did that too.

68
00:06:56,938 --> 00:07:00,548
Um Tae Bong, please find my father.

69
00:07:01,578 --> 00:07:04,618
Even so, how can she be so sincere about a misunderstanding?

70
00:07:04,948 --> 00:07:06,518
As if she really saw her father.

71
00:07:06,788 --> 00:07:08,088
I told you, right?

72
00:07:08,348 --> 00:07:10,618
Never go around alone.

73
00:07:11,018 --> 00:07:13,258
She has been like that since we first met.

74
00:07:14,158 --> 00:07:17,498
Like someone who actually knew me from before.

75
00:07:21,268 --> 00:07:22,368
My head hurts.

76
00:07:22,698 --> 00:07:24,198
It really hurts because of Cha Hong Du.

77
00:07:35,308 --> 00:07:37,648
Ruining the meal is all because of you, Father.

78
00:07:38,348 --> 00:07:41,488
Complaining about no side dishes, or dirt on the food...

79
00:07:43,218 --> 00:07:44,388
Just try yelling at me.

80
00:07:48,388 --> 00:07:50,798
If you do, I will ignore you even if you show up in my dreams.

81
00:07:55,668 --> 00:07:56,768
I mean it.

82
00:08:06,408 --> 00:08:07,408
No.

83
00:08:08,948 --> 00:08:09,978
I'm kidding.

84
00:08:12,218 --> 00:08:13,518
That was a lie.

85
00:08:17,418 --> 00:08:19,118
I won't ignore you.

86
00:08:22,858 --> 00:08:23,998
So...

87
00:08:26,668 --> 00:08:27,768
You have to come visit me...

88
00:08:29,328 --> 00:08:31,338
in my dreams, Dad.

89
00:08:35,008 --> 00:08:38,778
Then I won't just follow someone because they look like you.

90
00:08:40,508 --> 00:08:43,148
You are really gone now, right, Dad?

91
00:09:03,098 --> 00:09:05,838
He absolutely cannot sing.

92
00:09:05,898 --> 00:09:07,038
- Singing?
- Yes.

93
00:09:07,038 --> 00:09:08,138
(Hyun Ji's Happy Night)

94
00:09:08,138 --> 00:09:10,138
You get a free pass since you are Tae Bong's staff.

95
00:09:10,538 --> 00:09:12,538
Make sure to bring your ID next time.

96
00:09:12,608 --> 00:09:14,978
Yes, I understand.

97
00:09:15,048 --> 00:09:16,718
But you look a little different from yesterday.

98
00:09:17,118 --> 00:09:20,518
Your face looks puffy. Did you get Botox?

99
00:09:20,718 --> 00:09:22,618
- Excuse me?
- Can't you tell?

100
00:09:22,618 --> 00:09:24,818
Does that bouncy ball face look like Botox to you?

101
00:09:25,088 --> 00:09:26,158
Please...

102
00:09:28,888 --> 00:09:31,928
She is swollen from crying yesterday.

103
00:09:34,268 --> 00:09:36,498
Yes, the king of ratings, the master of romance,

104
00:09:36,568 --> 00:09:39,938
the ultimate heartthrob, Um Tae Bong, is here with us.

105
00:09:40,008 --> 00:09:42,538
You are currently in a very public relationship.

106
00:09:42,608 --> 00:09:45,408
Is it with the person we all know?

107
00:09:49,178 --> 00:09:52,418
I'm really curious about what made you fall for her.

108
00:09:52,478 --> 00:09:53,718
They are lasting longer than I thought.

109
00:09:54,448 --> 00:09:56,288
I thought he didn't really like...

110
00:09:56,348 --> 00:09:58,618
- Song Na Ri's type.
- Spill it. Tell us.

111
00:09:58,688 --> 00:10:00,958
Well, she...

112
00:10:01,828 --> 00:10:02,928
has pale skin...

113
00:10:04,258 --> 00:10:05,598
and long fingers?

114
00:10:06,398 --> 00:10:10,998
I thought a ring would look really good on those fingers.

115
00:10:12,198 --> 00:10:16,908
Oh my, does that mean you already have a ring ready for her?

116
00:10:18,638 --> 00:10:19,678
Maybe.

117
00:10:20,348 --> 00:10:23,878
Now, whether that lucky lady is the Na Ri we all know,

118
00:10:23,948 --> 00:10:27,818
or someone else entirely, well, we don't know yet.

119
00:10:27,888 --> 00:10:31,988
To all our female listeners out there, keep your hopes up.

120
00:10:32,118 --> 00:10:35,328
We will be right back after a song. Here is CNBLUE with "I Am A Loner."

121
00:10:37,598 --> 00:10:40,468
He does. He has had one since before he was famous.

122
00:10:40,528 --> 00:10:44,138
The One Ring, filled with all his years of sorrow.

123
00:10:44,998 --> 00:10:46,368
I guess he is going to propose with it later.

124
00:10:47,968 --> 00:10:48,968
Oh...

125
00:10:51,338 --> 00:10:53,648
I was wearing it without even knowing that.

126
00:11:04,258 --> 00:11:06,018
That is really bothering me.

127
00:11:08,128 --> 00:11:09,928
Oh, I'm sorry.

128
00:11:09,998 --> 00:11:12,158
How long is she going to stand there like that?

129
00:11:12,228 --> 00:11:13,898
It will be over soon.

130
00:11:21,808 --> 00:11:23,808
Are you not going to ask me to sing?

131
00:11:24,808 --> 00:11:25,808
Excuse me?

132
00:11:27,078 --> 00:11:28,308
Hey, the mic is still on.

133
00:11:29,308 --> 00:11:30,348
What is going on?

134
00:11:30,418 --> 00:11:31,778
(Making Him Sing Leads To Disaster)

135
00:11:32,818 --> 00:11:36,588
I smile a little so the tears will not fall

136
00:11:36,648 --> 00:11:40,228
Why are you doing this to me? What are you saying?

137
00:11:40,288 --> 00:11:44,128
All the words you said today up into the sky

138
00:11:44,198 --> 00:11:47,968
- The words I could never say - What's wrong with this?

139
00:11:48,028 --> 00:11:51,898
The words I never knew I would say while crying

140
00:11:51,968 --> 00:11:58,838
I like you so much

141
00:11:59,408 --> 00:12:00,878
What should I do?

142
00:12:02,908 --> 00:12:04,248
You idiot.

143
00:12:05,248 --> 00:12:09,388
Of all the songs, why did you pick the one with the three high notes?

144
00:12:09,448 --> 00:12:10,518
Um Tae Bong is completely tone-deaf.

145
00:12:10,588 --> 00:12:11,588
I thought it was a live mistake.

146
00:12:11,658 --> 00:12:12,658
I just spit out my food.

147
00:12:12,718 --> 00:12:15,658
The words I might never be able to say again

148
00:12:15,728 --> 00:12:22,328
I like you so much

149
00:12:22,398 --> 00:12:24,668
Goodness! One, two

150
00:12:24,738 --> 00:12:29,238
I'm in my dream

151
00:12:33,948 --> 00:12:35,348
Is it funny?

152
00:12:35,408 --> 00:12:36,678
I think so, maybe.

153
00:12:37,278 --> 00:12:38,578
Then it worked.

154
00:12:39,048 --> 00:12:40,188
Stop crying now.

155
00:12:40,688 --> 00:12:42,548
Even if something really worth crying about happens.

156
00:12:42,618 --> 00:12:44,558
Even if something really worth crying about happens?

157
00:12:45,318 --> 00:12:47,388
You are already not much to look at,

158
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:50,498
and you look even worse when you cry.

159
00:12:53,158 --> 00:12:54,668
Seriously, why did you do that earlier?

160
00:12:54,728 --> 00:12:56,938
Knowing it would cause a catastrophe like this.

161
00:12:58,568 --> 00:12:59,568
Tell me about it.

162
00:13:01,138 --> 00:13:02,168
(CEO Park)

163
00:13:07,748 --> 00:13:08,878
(CEO Park)

164
00:13:09,878 --> 00:13:12,548
Sir. We really tried our hardest to stop him.

165
00:13:12,618 --> 00:13:13,618
It is like he was possessed...

166
00:13:13,688 --> 00:13:15,618
No, it is fine. He did well.

167
00:13:15,688 --> 00:13:17,888
The internet is going absolutely crazy right now.

168
00:13:18,918 --> 00:13:20,388
Hey. Calls are coming in.

169
00:13:22,228 --> 00:13:24,658
"He is so bad at singing, it makes him more relatable."

170
00:13:24,858 --> 00:13:26,868
"I had given up on him, but today I'm a fan again."

171
00:13:26,928 --> 00:13:28,268
"My mom, who was suffering from depression,"

172
00:13:28,328 --> 00:13:30,638
"completely got over it thanks to Um Tae Bong's singing."

173
00:13:30,698 --> 00:13:32,068
Oh, the mood totally flipped.

174
00:13:32,138 --> 00:13:35,068
Tae Bong, but singing is really the one thing you cannot do.

175
00:13:35,138 --> 00:13:37,238
You would never sing even if your life depended on it.

176
00:13:37,308 --> 00:13:38,878
You have been acting really strange lately.

177
00:13:38,938 --> 00:13:40,448
I think so too.

178
00:13:45,548 --> 00:13:47,218
So, are you going to cure my motion sickness too?

179
00:13:54,688 --> 00:13:55,688
Darn it.

180
00:13:58,058 --> 00:13:59,358
That recording of my singing from earlier...

181
00:13:59,698 --> 00:14:01,568
People online said...

182
00:14:01,628 --> 00:14:04,198
that making it feel like you are not even in a car...

183
00:14:04,198 --> 00:14:05,868
is the best cure for motion sickness.

184
00:14:06,068 --> 00:14:07,408
How is it? Working like a charm, right?

185
00:14:07,538 --> 00:14:10,178
Welcome to the Um Tae Bong concert.

186
00:14:10,238 --> 00:14:12,708
You are killing me with this noise. A charm, my foot.

187
00:14:12,778 --> 00:14:14,378
You need a smack upside the head...

188
00:14:14,708 --> 00:14:15,748
Hey...

189
00:14:18,518 --> 00:14:19,518
Darn it...

190
00:14:30,398 --> 00:14:31,898
I think her motion sickness actually got better.

191
00:14:33,028 --> 00:14:36,168
Keep that with you at all times. If you lose it, you are dead.

192
00:14:40,538 --> 00:14:41,638
(CEO Park)

193
00:14:44,038 --> 00:14:46,608
What now? I thought the mood turned around.

194
00:14:49,178 --> 00:14:50,348
What is going on?

195
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:51,818
Anyway, getting off early is nice.

196
00:14:54,548 --> 00:14:56,888
What? Is the sky telling you something?

197
00:14:57,418 --> 00:14:58,488
Is it going to rain later?

198
00:14:59,718 --> 00:15:00,958
It's strange,

199
00:15:02,058 --> 00:15:03,488
but everything just feels so good.

200
00:15:04,298 --> 00:15:05,598
The sky,

201
00:15:07,468 --> 00:15:08,698
the air,

202
00:15:10,098 --> 00:15:11,498
the people,

203
00:15:12,038 --> 00:15:13,038
all of it.

204
00:15:14,838 --> 00:15:16,808
- I'm going to be late.
- Where are you going?

205
00:15:17,408 --> 00:15:19,838
The Haneul Columbarium. Yesterday was my father's memorial.

206
00:15:21,048 --> 00:15:23,378
For there, you see that bus stop over there?

207
00:15:23,618 --> 00:15:25,218
Take the 745 from there. It goes straight.

208
00:15:26,378 --> 00:15:27,748
How do you know all that?

209
00:15:28,118 --> 00:15:30,218
I go there a lot. Columbarium scenes in dramas...

210
00:15:30,288 --> 00:15:31,518
are almost always filmed there.

211
00:15:33,628 --> 00:15:35,358
- Go on, then.
- All right.

212
00:15:35,428 --> 00:15:36,458
Get home safe.

213
00:15:44,168 --> 00:15:46,898
I have the motion sickness cure Tae Bong gave me.

214
00:15:51,578 --> 00:15:54,148
Oh my, what in the world happened?

215
00:15:56,908 --> 00:15:58,978
To think the nation's father figure ended up like this.

216
00:15:59,048 --> 00:16:01,288
The patient probably will not remember you, Mr. Um.

217
00:16:01,688 --> 00:16:04,488
To be exact, he does not even remember...

218
00:16:04,558 --> 00:16:06,258
what kind of person he used to be.

219
00:16:11,298 --> 00:16:12,658
Sir.

220
00:16:13,668 --> 00:16:15,268
Do I smell?

221
00:16:16,468 --> 00:16:17,938
My daughter told me...

222
00:16:18,868 --> 00:16:20,368
that I smell like an old widower.

223
00:16:21,408 --> 00:16:24,078
I should change before she scolds me.

224
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:25,808
Have you seen my daughter?

225
00:16:26,078 --> 00:16:29,278
She is a huge fan of spicy rice cakes.

226
00:16:32,118 --> 00:16:33,348
Wait, no.

227
00:16:33,948 --> 00:16:36,418
My daughter hates spicy rice cakes.

228
00:16:42,128 --> 00:16:44,298
Some patients forget reality...

229
00:16:44,698 --> 00:16:47,098
and wish to live in a world of their own making.

230
00:16:47,568 --> 00:16:50,198
It is time for my daughter to come home.

231
00:16:51,768 --> 00:16:52,898
I need to go home.

232
00:16:52,968 --> 00:16:54,738
Mr. Choi is exactly that kind of case.

233
00:16:55,208 --> 00:16:57,908
He wants to live in a fictional world created by his dementia.

234
00:16:58,178 --> 00:17:01,508
That world is a mixture of dramas and reality.

235
00:17:01,578 --> 00:17:02,578
Sir.

236
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:08,518
It was freezing for a few days, but it is bearable today.

237
00:17:11,118 --> 00:17:12,918
From now on,

238
00:17:12,988 --> 00:17:15,828
- I will not be late.
- It is okay to be late sometimes.

239
00:17:16,688 --> 00:17:18,028
It is fine.

240
00:17:18,458 --> 00:17:20,398
Was his name Min Seok?

241
00:17:21,098 --> 00:17:24,238
I don't see the friend you used to hang around with.

242
00:17:28,808 --> 00:17:30,938
Have you heard the saying about the weight of the crown?

243
00:17:31,938 --> 00:17:35,008
Giving someone a proper send-off...

244
00:17:35,078 --> 00:17:36,908
is a way of enduring...

245
00:17:36,978 --> 00:17:38,348
that weight.

246
00:17:41,248 --> 00:17:42,888
All right, see you later.

247
00:17:44,888 --> 00:17:45,888
Sir.

248
00:17:48,058 --> 00:17:49,428
That...

249
00:17:49,488 --> 00:17:50,498
This.

250
00:17:53,658 --> 00:17:54,768
This morning,

251
00:17:56,968 --> 00:17:59,168
I sent my wife off.

252
00:18:00,938 --> 00:18:03,108
For the sake of those left behind,

253
00:18:03,168 --> 00:18:04,978
she left on a day that was not too cold.

254
00:18:07,278 --> 00:18:08,348
I'm grateful.

255
00:18:10,718 --> 00:18:12,848
She is someone to be grateful for.

256
00:18:30,738 --> 00:18:32,798
That is when you finally came to your senses.

257
00:18:34,538 --> 00:18:37,678
After you sent Min Seok off, you were living in a daze,

258
00:18:38,308 --> 00:18:40,848
but you said you snapped out of it after meeting Mr. Choi.

259
00:18:42,948 --> 00:18:43,978
I did.

260
00:18:45,048 --> 00:18:48,348
He lost his daughter in an accident not too long ago,

261
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:50,558
and it seems his condition worsened suddenly.

262
00:18:50,618 --> 00:18:51,618
The doctor said...

263
00:18:51,688 --> 00:18:54,758
he keeps trying to go back to the time...

264
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:56,658
when he lived with his wife and daughter.

265
00:18:56,728 --> 00:18:59,798
That must be the time he wants to remember the most.

266
00:18:59,858 --> 00:19:01,768
Even yesterday, he was wandering around...

267
00:19:01,768 --> 00:19:03,028
in front of his daughter's old school,

268
00:19:03,098 --> 00:19:04,738
and it seems our staff brought him back.

269
