And the name Cha Hong Du is the female lead...

530
00:37:03,548 --> 00:37:05,418
from "The Crown Prince's Bodyguard" that we filmed together.

531
00:37:12,888 --> 00:37:17,858
("The Crown Prince's Bodyguard")

532
00:37:19,958 --> 00:37:21,598
(Song Na Ri As Cha Hong Du)

533
00:37:23,698 --> 00:37:25,998
No wonder that name sounded so familiar...

534
00:37:26,698 --> 00:37:28,868
No way. It must be a coincidence.

535
00:37:30,168 --> 00:37:32,708
Anyway, it is a relief she is not your bodyguard.

536
00:37:32,778 --> 00:37:34,538
If she were, it would be just like the drama,

537
00:37:34,608 --> 00:37:36,408
meaning she totally planned to get close to you.

538
00:37:38,078 --> 00:37:39,918
To call that a coincidence too...

539
00:37:41,588 --> 00:37:42,818
No way.

540
00:37:51,798 --> 00:37:52,828
You.

541
00:37:53,728 --> 00:37:54,898
Do you like me?

542
00:37:57,498 --> 00:37:59,398
Are you crazy? Why would I like you?

543
00:37:59,468 --> 00:38:00,668
Hey!

544
00:38:00,668 --> 00:38:02,468
That's gross! Get me a tissue.

545
00:38:03,338 --> 00:38:04,708
Get me a wet wipe.

546
00:38:07,608 --> 00:38:09,148
- She doesn't seem...
- Ma'am, can I get a wet wipe?

547
00:38:09,148 --> 00:38:10,248
like an obsessive fangirl...

548
00:38:11,248 --> 00:38:12,318
(I Will Ruin Your Career)

549
00:38:12,378 --> 00:38:15,018
What a crazy jerk. Are you not going to report this?

550
00:38:15,088 --> 00:38:16,288
Are you not reporting this?

551
00:38:16,348 --> 00:38:20,218
We should catch him and squeeze the ink right out of his eyes...

552
00:38:20,288 --> 00:38:23,188
so he comes to his senses and never sends this kind of thing again.

553
00:38:23,388 --> 00:38:25,458
Watch your back at night, my foot.

554
00:38:25,528 --> 00:38:27,328
Should you not be protecting your artist?

555
00:38:27,398 --> 00:38:29,998
She does not seem like an anti-fan either...

556
00:38:38,878 --> 00:38:40,608
Watch out. Coming through.

557
00:38:50,188 --> 00:38:53,658
What? Why is she so unathletic?

558
00:38:57,988 --> 00:38:59,198
Then again,

559
00:38:59,258 --> 00:39:01,498
she did call herself a martial artist or whatever.

560
00:39:01,558 --> 00:39:04,128
I didn't actually see her catch that guy.

561
00:39:04,198 --> 00:39:07,198
Looking at her now, she is terrible at physical stuff.

562
00:39:07,738 --> 00:39:10,368
If she is not a die-hard fan trying to stick by my side...

563
00:39:10,438 --> 00:39:13,538
or an anti-fan trying to find my weakness and sell it,

564
00:39:14,538 --> 00:39:16,878
why did she insist on being my bodyguard?

565
00:39:22,048 --> 00:39:24,288
- What are you doing?
- Gosh, you startled me.

566
00:39:24,348 --> 00:39:25,518
I almost hit you, man.

567
00:39:27,888 --> 00:39:28,888
But Tae Bong.

568
00:39:28,958 --> 00:39:32,128
You keep watching Cha Hong Du like this...

569
00:39:33,298 --> 00:39:34,398
Did you lend her money?

570
00:39:36,528 --> 00:39:37,868
- Su Dong.
- Yes.

571
00:39:38,738 --> 00:39:40,138
Let's drink some coffee.

572
00:39:40,198 --> 00:39:41,198
Okay.

573
00:39:43,768 --> 00:39:45,678
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

574
00:39:47,808 --> 00:39:49,578
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

575
00:39:52,278 --> 00:39:53,618
Aren't you sick of that?

576
00:39:53,778 --> 00:39:57,448
If you are sick of it, you can change it to another song yourself.

577
00:39:57,518 --> 00:39:58,618
No,

578
00:39:59,418 --> 00:40:00,588
I like this song.

579
00:40:01,688 --> 00:40:03,858
All right, then. See you later.

580
00:40:07,198 --> 00:40:10,468
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

581
00:40:14,198 --> 00:40:15,838
He could have at least fed me dinner before sending me off.

582
00:40:17,908 --> 00:40:19,338
What should I have for a meal today?

583
00:40:21,108 --> 00:40:22,778
Gosh, I'm hungry.

584
00:40:33,458 --> 00:40:34,488
I'm finally a bit full.

585
00:40:36,188 --> 00:40:39,498
But when are you going to teach me how to drink?

586
00:40:41,828 --> 00:40:45,868
On a day when you are so lonely you really crave a drink?

587
00:40:46,598 --> 00:40:49,238
Then I will never learn how to drink.

588
00:40:50,338 --> 00:40:51,338
That's sad.

589
00:40:54,008 --> 00:40:55,378
I have never been lonely.

590
00:40:55,648 --> 00:40:57,948
Really? Not even once in your life?

591
00:40:59,218 --> 00:41:02,788
I received a lot of love from my father growing up,

592
00:41:02,848 --> 00:41:05,888
and I was super busy working part-time jobs.

593
00:41:06,158 --> 00:41:07,288
I'm jealous.

594
00:41:07,788 --> 00:41:08,958
I have been lonely a lot.

595
00:41:09,828 --> 00:41:12,258
When we immigrated to the UK, I had no friends,

596
00:41:12,458 --> 00:41:13,628
and I couldn't speak the language.

597
00:41:14,898 --> 00:41:18,568
You can stay by yourself until Mom and Dad get back from work, right?

598
00:41:18,968 --> 00:41:21,368
Make sure to turn off the lights so the neighbours don't see.

599
00:41:23,568 --> 00:41:25,608
I was afraid my parents would worry if they knew,

600
00:41:25,908 --> 00:41:27,808
so I hid those feelings completely.

601
00:41:28,408 --> 00:41:30,178
I guess you could say I grew up too fast.

602
00:41:30,878 --> 00:41:32,518
You must have missed Korea a lot.

603
00:41:37,048 --> 00:41:40,758
Is that why I care about her more?

604
00:41:42,388 --> 00:41:43,388
Her?

605
00:41:44,628 --> 00:41:45,898
A certain woman.

606
00:41:46,528 --> 00:41:48,868
Because I thought she might be like how I used to be.

607
00:41:49,868 --> 00:41:51,938
Who is this woman all of a sudden?

608
00:41:52,598 --> 00:41:54,368
Is she cooler than me?

609
00:41:55,508 --> 00:41:56,838
I don't know about that,

610
00:41:57,668 --> 00:42:01,438
but I know she's completely different from you, Hong Du.

611
00:42:02,648 --> 00:42:04,308
Completely different from me?

612
00:42:05,478 --> 00:42:06,548
She doesn't have any friends.

613
00:42:10,988 --> 00:42:13,318
That kind of tells you how she's lived her life.

614
00:42:14,718 --> 00:42:17,758
People get hurt by the ones closest to them,

615
00:42:18,288 --> 00:42:19,858
but they also get healed by them.

616
00:42:21,058 --> 00:42:22,998
It seems like she never even had that chance.

617
00:42:25,098 --> 00:42:26,768
So I really want to meet her.

618
00:42:28,368 --> 00:42:30,208
I feel like we'd be good friends.

619
00:42:32,478 --> 00:42:34,178
And there's a reason I have to.

620
00:42:34,238 --> 00:42:38,448
I don't even know who she is, but I'm starting to get jealous.

621
00:42:43,888 --> 00:42:46,258
By the way, isn't our rooftop place great?

622
00:42:46,258 --> 00:42:47,788
It really is.

623
00:42:51,258 --> 00:42:52,298
Really?

624
00:42:52,858 --> 00:42:55,628
Please keep taking good care of Mr. Choi.

625
00:43:04,868 --> 00:43:06,308
(The Crown Prince's Bodyguard)

626
00:43:11,108 --> 00:43:14,018
What? You want me to smile again?

627
00:43:15,348 --> 00:43:16,348
I know.

628
00:43:17,818 --> 00:43:18,918
You should have lived longer.

629
00:43:20,058 --> 00:43:21,518
It's become a drama...

630
00:43:23,858 --> 00:43:25,258
I intentionally want to forget...

631
00:43:25,258 --> 00:43:26,528
because it keeps making me think of you.

632
00:43:30,798 --> 00:43:33,898
("The Crown Prince's Bodyguard")

633
00:43:37,608 --> 00:43:39,538
I will pay you whatever salary you want.

634
00:43:39,608 --> 00:43:41,738
You start the day you leave the hospital.

635
00:43:42,308 --> 00:43:44,708
I'm all better. I'll start right away.

636
00:43:45,818 --> 00:43:47,118
Is she a doctor or something?

637
00:43:47,178 --> 00:43:49,018
Taking off her bandages however she wants.

638
00:43:49,648 --> 00:43:51,518
Creepy. How do I know this?

639
00:43:51,518 --> 00:43:52,718
Are you still going to ignore me?

640
00:43:53,358 --> 00:43:54,858
It's exactly like the drama.

641
00:43:56,688 --> 00:43:58,258
Then was all of that...

642
00:43:59,898 --> 00:44:01,858
just lines from the drama?

643
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:03,598
She really...

644
00:44:05,298 --> 00:44:08,938
acted like it happened to her.

645
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:14,008
You didn't have to walk me home.

646
00:44:14,508 --> 00:44:16,008
We're here. This is my place.

647
00:44:16,148 --> 00:44:18,508
Wow, you live in a really nice place.

648
00:44:19,118 --> 00:44:20,418
Man, I want to live somewhere like this.

649
00:44:22,988 --> 00:44:23,988
Oh?

650
00:44:28,258 --> 00:44:29,758
- Hello?
- What are you doing tomorrow?

651
00:44:30,258 --> 00:44:32,258
I'll head in first. Take your time.

652
00:44:34,958 --> 00:44:37,428
- Is someone with you?
- Why did you call?

653
00:44:37,498 --> 00:44:38,498
Come out tomorrow.

654
00:44:38,568 --> 00:44:40,638
Why? You don't have a shoot tomorrow.

655
00:44:40,698 --> 00:44:41,768
There's something I need to check.

656
00:44:46,238 --> 00:44:47,678
("The Crown Prince's Bodyguard")

657
00:44:56,918 --> 00:44:59,218
You're just going to blatantly use me as your stylist, aren't you?

658
00:44:59,688 --> 00:45:01,058
Are you going to pay me double then?

659
00:45:01,118 --> 00:45:02,488
Carry these and follow me.

660
00:45:02,558 --> 00:45:04,028
Did you not call me to check something?

661
00:45:04,088 --> 00:45:06,728
What are you checking? What? How strong I'm?

662
00:45:10,598 --> 00:45:12,998
Bodyguard rule number one.

663
00:45:15,168 --> 00:45:17,338
No matter what, you must not look like a bodyguard.

664
00:45:18,338 --> 00:45:19,638
Is that why you're making me carry your bags?

665
00:45:19,708 --> 00:45:20,708
Then you're wrong.

666
00:45:22,878 --> 00:45:24,978
Because I have the kind of face that looks cool no matter what I do.

667
00:45:29,718 --> 00:45:31,388
That sounds really familiar.

668
00:45:31,448 --> 00:45:32,788
Is that why you're making me carry your bags?

669
00:45:33,588 --> 00:45:34,788
How many times do I have to tell you?

670
00:45:34,858 --> 00:45:38,388
I have the kind of face that looks cool no matter what I do.

671
00:45:39,028 --> 00:45:41,458
She said that exactly like the drama too.

672
00:45:50,208 --> 00:45:51,638
What do you need to check?

673
00:45:51,708 --> 00:45:53,438
What? How popular you are?

674
00:45:53,438 --> 00:45:55,408
Bodyguard rule number two.

675
00:45:57,408 --> 00:46:00,778
The more you stand out to people, the less suspicious you become.

676
00:46:01,448 --> 00:46:04,648
Then wouldn't a more common dish be better?

677
00:46:05,048 --> 00:46:07,058
Like beef, for example?

678
00:46:09,188 --> 00:46:11,158
Gosh, you forgot again.

679
00:46:11,888 --> 00:46:15,398
I told you, you need a more common menu for times like this.

680
00:46:15,468 --> 00:46:17,128
Like beef, for example?

681
00:46:21,398 --> 00:46:22,868
She could just be copying it.

682
00:46:23,908 --> 00:46:26,238
If she just memorized the lines by heart...

683
00:46:36,018 --> 00:46:37,018
Are you okay?

684
00:46:37,388 --> 00:46:39,118
Hey, can't you see someone standing here?

685
00:46:39,388 --> 00:46:41,918
- I'm sorry.
- Where are your eyes?

686
00:46:41,918 --> 00:46:43,528
- She protected me again.
- That was almost a disaster.

687
00:46:44,058 --> 00:46:45,828
This is not something you can just copy.

688
00:46:46,158 --> 00:46:48,398
It only happens if you truly believe it.

689
00:46:48,458 --> 00:46:49,468
Hong Du.

690
00:46:51,668 --> 00:46:53,398
Tae Bong is here, too.

691
00:46:54,038 --> 00:46:55,268
How did you two...

692
00:47:01,478 --> 00:47:03,608
The terrible employer Hong Du mentioned...

693
00:47:03,608 --> 00:47:05,208
was this close all along.

694
00:47:08,548 --> 00:47:11,488
Actually, I went to the sandwich shop earlier...

695
00:47:11,548 --> 00:47:15,018
just in case, since it is your favourite place.

696
00:47:15,458 --> 00:47:17,088
I thought if I ran into you,

697
00:47:18,228 --> 00:47:19,658
it might mean we are destined.

698
00:47:21,458 --> 00:47:22,468
What?

699
00:47:24,898 --> 00:47:27,598
I'm joking, don't be so scared.

700
00:47:28,098 --> 00:47:30,868
It must be nice having such a huge fan by your side.

701
00:47:31,338 --> 00:47:33,608
I had a really funny thought earlier.

702
00:47:34,278 --> 00:47:36,608
Even if we ignore the name Cha Hong Du,

703
00:47:36,678 --> 00:47:39,048
the story about her late father and stepmother...

704
00:47:39,118 --> 00:47:41,448
is exactly the same as the drama's plot.

705
00:47:41,718 --> 00:47:45,088
But it turns out she did all that just to catch your attention.

706
00:47:45,348 --> 00:47:46,918
Playing the tragic heroine.

707
00:47:47,388 --> 00:47:50,728
But that didn't sit right with me.

708
00:47:55,768 --> 00:47:58,998
He calls me out here and just acts all serious by himself all day.

709
00:47:59,368 --> 00:48:01,768
He leaves without even telling me what he confirmed.

710
00:48:02,138 --> 00:48:05,408
Anyway, Um Tae Bong was really weird today.

711
00:48:07,608 --> 00:48:08,708
By the way,

712
00:48:09,378 --> 00:48:11,548
he seems really close with that pretty girl.

713
00:48:18,148 --> 00:48:20,718
Darn it, you stupid idiot.

714
00:48:20,788 --> 00:48:22,888
Even Hyun Joo found it weird, and only I didn't know.

715
00:48:23,488 --> 00:48:25,798
The story about her late father and stepmother...

716
00:48:25,858 --> 00:48:28,158
is exactly the same as the drama's plot.

717
00:48:28,698 --> 00:48:29,928
There is no way...

718
00:48:30,598 --> 00:48:33,238
she would've made up a story about her father.

719
00:48:33,298 --> 00:48:35,638
Han Jung Woo, no, Um Tae Bong.

720
00:48:35,638 --> 00:48:39,708
Please, find my father.

721
00:48:40,138 --> 00:48:43,778
Oh, she definitely called me Han Jung Woo back then.

722
00:48:43,848 --> 00:48:45,578
I'm a bodyguard.

723
00:48:46,318 --> 00:48:48,748
Your secret bodyguard,

724
00:48:48,818 --> 00:48:51,648
Cha Hong Du.

725
00:48:51,948 --> 00:48:53,258
Does she really believe...

726
00:48:54,288 --> 00:48:56,458
she is a character in a drama?

727
00:48:57,228 --> 00:48:58,258
Darn it.

728
00:49:06,338 --> 00:49:07,438
Darn it.

729
00:49:12,338 --> 00:49:13,408
Is this...

730
00:49:14,538 --> 00:49:16,208
seriously the only way?

731
00:49:28,158 --> 00:49:29,358
What do you want to talk about?

732
00:49:32,898 --> 00:49:34,498
You called me all the way out here,

733
00:49:34,558 --> 00:49:36,468
so are we going to have a staring contest this time?

734
00:49:36,528 --> 00:49:38,098
If you were just my stalker...

735
00:49:38,168 --> 00:49:40,538
and you were the one who sent those letters,

736
00:49:41,068 --> 00:49:43,068
I would have tried to reconsider somehow.

737
00:49:43,138 --> 00:49:44,708
Because at least that makes sense.

738
00:49:46,778 --> 00:49:48,138
Speak so I can understand you.

739
00:49:48,208 --> 00:49:50,778
If you approached me to dig up my secrets,

740
00:49:50,848 --> 00:49:53,118
and that was why you stuck by my side,

741
00:49:53,318 --> 00:49:54,318
I thought about smacking you once...

742
00:49:54,378 --> 00:49:56,488
and accepting you as my person. But...

743
00:49:58,388 --> 00:49:59,458
If it is not even that...

744
00:49:59,518 --> 00:50:01,058
Was there not an incident like that before?

745
00:50:01,118 --> 00:50:03,758
Some woman couldn't tell a drama from reality,

746
00:50:03,828 --> 00:50:05,228
so she went to find her favourite celebrity...

747
00:50:05,288 --> 00:50:07,028
and made a scene, claiming they were married...

748
00:50:07,028 --> 00:50:08,058
and that she was having his baby.

749
00:50:08,128 --> 00:50:12,098
So there is someone exactly like that right in front of me.

750
00:50:12,168 --> 00:50:14,698
People with harsh realities and hard lives do that.

751
00:50:14,768 --> 00:50:17,108
They just want to forget reality, even if it means doing that.

752
00:50:17,168 --> 00:50:19,278
I feel really bad for people like that.

753
00:50:19,338 --> 00:50:20,778
But what a shame.

754
00:50:20,838 --> 00:50:22,878
I don't feel bad for you at all.

755
00:50:23,608 --> 00:50:25,848
What have you been talking about this whole time?

756
00:50:30,788 --> 00:50:31,788
You are fired.

757
00:50:33,658 --> 00:50:34,658
What?

758
00:50:35,888 --> 00:50:37,158
I'm completely sick of you.

759
00:50:38,158 --> 00:50:39,758
- What?
- You,

760
00:50:41,058 --> 00:50:42,898
get out of my life.

761
00:50:59,378 --> 00:51:02,588
He should at least tell me what I did wrong so I know.

762
00:51:03,188 --> 00:51:04,388
I'm completely sick of you.

763
00:51:08,358 --> 00:51:09,358
Jerk.

764
00:51:11,088 --> 00:51:12,128
He didn't have to...

765
00:51:13,528 --> 00:51:14,558
say it so harshly.

766
00:51:20,398 --> 00:51:22,968
For someone who became so successful,

767
00:51:23,038 --> 00:51:24,738
why did the look in your eyes change so much?

768
00:51:27,408 --> 00:51:29,008
You have the loneliest eyes in the world.

769
00:51:30,078 --> 00:51:32,418
She can't even take care of herself, yet acts like she knows everything.

770
00:51:41,388 --> 00:51:43,188
Son, did you eat?

771
00:51:44,058 --> 00:51:45,058
Hey, Dad.

772
00:51:45,058 --> 00:51:47,098
Yes, I think I'll finish early today.

773
00:51:47,298 --> 00:51:48,758
Want to get chicken and beer with your daughter?

774
00:51:50,298 --> 00:51:52,568
Cha Hong Du, let's eat.

775
00:52:01,778 --> 00:52:03,448
It does not matter if she eats or not anymore.

776
00:52:04,708 --> 00:52:05,948
I told you, right?

777
00:52:06,148 --> 00:52:07,318
That I would always...

778
00:52:08,618 --> 00:52:09,788
protect you.

779
00:52:19,898 --> 00:52:22,968
If you're not Cha Hong Du, what is your real name?

780
00:52:24,268 --> 00:52:25,268
Darn it.

781
00:52:38,908 --> 00:52:40,548
Get your hands off her right now.

782
00:52:40,618 --> 00:52:41,948
- Whoa, you scared me.
- Oh, you scared me.

783
00:52:42,018 --> 00:52:43,048
(Neighbourhood Fried Chicken)

784
00:52:43,588 --> 00:52:44,848
The person you saw earlier...

785
00:52:44,848 --> 00:52:46,918
What was he wearing? Tell me in detail.

786
00:52:49,188 --> 00:52:50,888
Cha Hong Du, let's eat.

787
00:52:55,758 --> 00:52:57,128
It's gone again.

788
00:52:59,768 --> 00:53:00,868
My job...

789
00:53:04,238 --> 00:53:05,808
The person who makes me laugh...

790
00:53:08,608 --> 00:53:11,108
The person who asks me to eat with him...

791
00:53:18,848 --> 00:53:19,888
Here...

792
00:53:20,988 --> 00:53:21,988
I added a little extra.

793
00:53:23,428 --> 00:53:24,428
Take it.

794
00:53:26,128 --> 00:53:27,998
That guy is pretty fickle.

795
00:53:28,658 --> 00:53:30,198
Please try to understand, Hong Du.

796
00:53:30,628 --> 00:53:31,628
Okay.

797
00:53:32,168 --> 00:53:34,098
But you will need to find a new bodyguard, right?

798
00:53:34,538 --> 00:53:36,868
Oh, why are you worrying about the guy who just fired you?

799
00:53:36,938 --> 00:53:38,438
It's fine. He will figure it out himself.

800
00:53:40,238 --> 00:53:41,238
Right.

801
00:53:43,308 --> 00:53:44,548
Here.

802
00:53:45,078 --> 00:53:46,578
Um Tae Bong gave this to me.

803
00:53:46,918 --> 00:53:48,518
Since I'm not his bodyguard anymore.

804
00:53:49,048 --> 00:53:50,188
But...

805
00:53:50,588 --> 00:53:53,088
Please tell him I can't return the motion sickness medicine.

806
00:53:54,788 --> 00:53:56,128
Motion sickness medicine?

807
00:53:56,188 --> 00:53:58,628
I can't ride in a car without it now.

808
00:53:58,688 --> 00:54:00,258
Tae Bong gave you that too?

809
00:54:00,328 --> 00:54:01,628
He gave you all sorts of things.

810
00:54:01,928 --> 00:54:03,698
He is not the type to just give his things away to others.

811
00:54:04,898 --> 00:54:07,198
Well, goodbye then.

812
00:54:07,838 --> 00:54:09,138
Thank you for everything.

813
00:54:20,178 --> 00:54:21,578
Do you feel relieved?

814
00:54:24,088 --> 00:54:25,618
I will go buy something cold to drink.

815
00:54:43,268 --> 00:54:45,738
Do you remember my voice?

816
00:54:48,308 --> 00:54:49,348
The blank check?

817
00:55:00,818 --> 00:55:01,918
(CEO's Office)

818
00:55:03,328 --> 00:55:04,328
Why are you empty-handed?

819
00:55:05,358 --> 00:55:07,728
Would it have been better to call the police?

820
00:55:08,228 --> 00:55:10,028
She could have been a crazy stalker.

821
00:55:10,528 --> 00:55:11,528
Hey.

822
00:55:13,898 --> 00:55:15,838
We need to bring Cha Hong Du back.

823
00:55:16,208 --> 00:55:17,668
Bring her back?

824
00:55:17,908 --> 00:55:21,178
- I barely got rid of her.
- No. You have to keep her close.

825
00:55:21,438 --> 00:55:23,348
- What are you talking about?
- She knows.

826
00:55:24,108 --> 00:55:25,608
She knows your secret.

827
00:55:26,618 --> 00:55:27,618
(Blank Check)

828
00:55:30,018 --> 00:55:31,348
A blank check?

829
00:55:31,888 --> 00:55:33,358
Just let her believe what she wants...

830
00:55:33,888 --> 00:55:36,928
and keep her by Um Tae Bong's side.

831
00:55:40,728 --> 00:55:44,828
Is she the sick person you mentioned last time...

832
00:55:44,898 --> 00:55:46,668
The one with a lot of money...

833
00:55:48,238 --> 00:55:51,208
I see. I will get hurt if I know too much.

834
00:55:51,208 --> 00:55:52,208
But how do I do that?

835
00:55:52,208 --> 00:55:55,238
Tae Bong is pretty quick to catch on.

836
00:55:55,308 --> 00:55:57,608
I trust you will figure that out.

837
00:55:57,608 --> 00:55:59,678
No one can know about our deal.

838
00:56:00,378 --> 00:56:01,618
Not even Um Tae Bong.

839
00:56:04,448 --> 00:56:06,258
No, she can't know.

840
00:56:07,588 --> 00:56:08,858
There is no way she knows.

841
00:56:08,918 --> 00:56:10,188
She threatened me.

842
00:56:17,198 --> 00:56:18,298
So...

843
00:56:18,368 --> 00:56:20,598
- For now, just do as she says...
- No.

844
00:56:21,098 --> 00:56:22,438
She was weird from the start.

845
00:56:22,438 --> 00:56:23,608
She showed up out of nowhere one day...

846
00:56:23,668 --> 00:56:25,968
and started acting like the main character in my drama for no reason.

847
00:56:26,708 --> 00:56:28,278
What kind of massive shock did she go through?

848
00:56:29,678 --> 00:56:32,548
Cha Hong Du, what in the world happened to you?

849
00:56:33,348 --> 00:56:34,948
She must have her reasons.

850
00:56:35,348 --> 00:56:37,088
She might have been really lonely.

851
00:56:37,088 --> 00:56:38,648
I told you before.

852
00:56:38,718 --> 00:56:41,358
When you are lonely, it hurts right here.

853
00:56:41,888 --> 00:56:43,658
Or is it here? It could hurt here too.

854
00:56:43,728 --> 00:56:45,058
If she is hurting,

855
00:56:45,128 --> 00:56:47,558
is she more likely to cause trouble?

856
00:56:47,628 --> 00:56:50,628
Of course. So for the time being...

857
00:56:51,098 --> 00:56:53,398
let's just play along with whatever she wants to believe.

858
00:56:53,468 --> 00:56:54,698
This is driving me crazy.

859
00:56:54,698 --> 00:56:57,308
Why does she have to know?

860
00:57:03,508 --> 00:57:04,508
But...

861
00:57:08,148 --> 00:57:10,588
Are you sure that she...

862
00:57:11,118 --> 00:57:12,418
threatened you?

863
00:57:17,428 --> 00:57:18,428
Hey,

864
00:57:19,898 --> 00:57:20,898
do you not trust me?

865
00:57:23,828 --> 00:57:24,828
Do I...

866
00:57:26,368 --> 00:57:28,098
look like someone who would lie to you?

867
00:57:36,648 --> 00:57:37,648
Darn it, seriously.

868
00:57:45,988 --> 00:57:47,318
This is driving me crazy.

869
00:57:47,818 --> 00:57:48,888
Right.

870
00:57:49,988 --> 00:57:51,158
Let's sweep it all away.

871
00:57:51,558 --> 00:57:55,258
Sweep the streets, and sweep my heart.

872
00:57:56,398 --> 00:57:59,998
I will sweep away all the arrogant jerks in the world too.

873
00:58:00,098 --> 00:58:01,468
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

874
00:58:04,908 --> 00:58:06,138
Darn it.

875
00:58:12,348 --> 00:58:13,818
Why won't this come off?

876
00:58:26,028 --> 00:58:27,228
Darn it.

877
00:58:28,498 --> 00:58:29,798
Are you doing a horror movie now? Are you playing a zombie?

878
00:58:29,868 --> 00:58:31,068
Make it quick, my noodles are boiling.

879
00:58:31,068 --> 00:58:34,998
You jerk. Are you more worried about soggy noodles than my life?

880
00:58:35,068 --> 00:58:36,068
Is it a girl problem?

881
00:58:36,138 --> 00:58:37,738
Do I look like someone who would cause that kind of problem...

882
00:58:40,978 --> 00:58:42,638
Sometimes...

883
00:58:42,708 --> 00:58:45,548
- I'm that kind of person.
- I don't know what it is,

884
00:58:46,008 --> 00:58:47,918
but as long as you did nothing to take responsibility for, it is fine.

885
00:58:47,978 --> 00:58:51,018
The problem is something happened I have to take responsibility for.

886
00:58:53,588 --> 00:58:55,218
Did you get someone pregnant?

887
00:58:55,288 --> 00:58:57,458
- Do you want to die?
- Do you want to get hit?

888
00:58:58,158 --> 00:58:59,158
Anyway.

889
00:59:00,498 --> 00:59:02,498
Hey, let's say...

890
00:59:02,558 --> 00:59:05,198
you know some fatal information about me.

891
00:59:05,268 --> 00:59:06,268
Is it worth money?

892
00:59:07,768 --> 00:59:08,768
Get out.

893
00:59:08,838 --> 00:59:10,608
What is the number for Distouch? You know a reporter, right?

894
00:59:10,668 --> 00:59:12,568
- Get out. Get out.
- One with a big mouth.

895
00:59:12,638 --> 00:59:13,838
Just go boil your noodles.

896
00:59:14,908 --> 00:59:17,778
They say there is a law of total madness for humans.

897
00:59:17,848 --> 00:59:20,718
Of course, your total madness is probably higher than normal people.

898
00:59:20,978 --> 00:59:22,178
But don't take that madness...

899
00:59:23,848 --> 00:59:25,018
out on Hyun Joo.

900
00:59:28,458 --> 00:59:29,628
Hey, what does that mean?

901
00:59:30,958 --> 00:59:32,128
Tell me before you go.

902
00:59:32,558 --> 00:59:33,558
Darn it.

903
00:59:43,808 --> 00:59:45,268
You have to solve it.

904
00:59:45,908 --> 00:59:47,808
So, Cha Hong Du.

905
00:59:47,878 --> 00:59:50,778
No, the one who believes she is Cha Hong Du...

906
00:59:50,848 --> 00:59:53,978
I just have to pretend it is real according to her delusion?

907
00:59:54,748 --> 00:59:55,748
Darn it.

908
00:59:57,288 --> 00:59:59,048
What, is this the "Truman Show" now?

909
00:59:59,118 --> 01:00:00,658
Am I supposed to shoot a drama just for her?

910
01:00:04,488 --> 01:00:07,898
I thought that crazy stalker was quiet lately,

911
01:00:08,198 --> 01:00:10,498
now there is someone blackmailing me with my secret.

912
01:00:11,668 --> 01:00:13,368
Does she think I will call her back because of that?

913
01:00:14,998 --> 01:00:17,168
Do you know what the scariest thing in the world is?

914
01:00:17,238 --> 01:00:19,838
What, an edgy teenager? No.

915
01:00:20,038 --> 01:00:21,278
People who are weird up here.

916
01:00:21,338 --> 01:00:23,108
Why? Because they are unpredictable.

917
01:00:31,948 --> 01:00:34,258
There was a reason her face was so bright.

918
01:00:34,518 --> 01:00:36,658
It was because she has an unpredictable brain.

919
01:00:37,988 --> 01:00:40,558
I'm still not going to do it. I will never call her.

920
01:00:41,728 --> 01:00:42,798
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

921
01:00:43,128 --> 01:00:44,768
Chicken...

922
01:00:44,828 --> 01:00:46,198
This is the right place...

923
01:00:47,768 --> 01:00:49,768
Darn it. Gosh.

924
01:00:56,308 --> 01:00:57,378
Why are you here?

925
01:00:58,148 --> 01:01:00,618
Don't tell me you want the motion sickness medicine back?

926
01:01:02,318 --> 01:01:04,488
This is so petty.

927
01:01:05,648 --> 01:01:07,458
Come back to work starting tomorrow.

928
01:01:08,058 --> 01:01:09,088
I think I...

929
01:01:10,028 --> 01:01:11,658
made a mistake.

930
01:01:13,598 --> 01:01:14,928
I thought you lost all affection for me.

931
01:01:16,258 --> 01:01:17,268
Me?

932
01:01:18,268 --> 01:01:20,198
If I really did,

933
01:01:20,468 --> 01:01:23,568
give me a chance to apologize.

934
01:01:26,738 --> 01:01:29,078
Why did you suddenly change your mind?

935
01:01:29,638 --> 01:01:31,178
Are you asking me that?

936
01:01:34,618 --> 01:01:37,818
She wanted you, Tae Bong, to never know she blackmailed you.

937
01:01:39,988 --> 01:01:41,088
Just because.

938
01:01:41,158 --> 01:01:43,488
There is a good phrase in the world called "just because."

939
01:01:43,758 --> 01:01:45,928
Just live, just work, just like it.

940
01:01:52,568 --> 01:01:53,768
The last one...

941
01:01:56,068 --> 01:01:57,208
was not a good example.

942
01:01:59,508 --> 01:02:01,238
Did anyone say anything?

943
01:02:04,878 --> 01:02:05,978
You...

944
01:02:06,748 --> 01:02:09,278
When you said you did not know my secret,

945
01:02:10,448 --> 01:02:11,448
was that true?

946
01:02:12,648 --> 01:02:13,958
- Why?
- Answer me.

947
01:02:15,058 --> 01:02:16,058
I don't know.

948
01:02:20,428 --> 01:02:21,428
Darn it.

949
01:02:22,628 --> 01:02:24,698
Anyway, I said it.

950
01:02:24,768 --> 01:02:26,098
Keep working.

951
01:02:29,738 --> 01:02:31,438
What? Do you not want to?

952
01:02:32,568 --> 01:02:35,308
Who said I didn't want to? I want to, absolutely.

953
01:02:36,778 --> 01:02:39,108
I really want to.

954
01:03:03,968 --> 01:03:07,038
Right, I hired her back. I did.

955
01:03:07,438 --> 01:03:09,478
So what am I supposed to do now?

956
01:03:10,108 --> 01:03:12,408
Is it enough to just let her stay by my side?

957
01:03:18,788 --> 01:03:20,588
Should I give this back first?

958
01:03:21,688 --> 01:03:22,918
Darn it.

959
01:03:25,188 --> 01:03:26,428
So fickle.

960
01:03:26,928 --> 01:03:29,558
Well, I will let it slide just this one time.

961
01:03:30,628 --> 01:03:31,628
Just because.

962
01:03:31,698 --> 01:03:33,998
There is a good phrase in the world called "just because."

963
01:03:34,068 --> 01:03:36,338
Just live, just work, just like it.

964
01:03:47,448 --> 01:03:48,818
Why is my heart beating so fast?

965
01:03:50,088 --> 01:03:51,518
Is it beating just because, too?

966
01:04:04,098 --> 01:04:05,668
(Name: Choi Gu)

967
01:04:05,828 --> 01:04:08,568
- Where did the patient here go?
- He was here just a moment ago.

968
01:04:08,638 --> 01:04:10,808
- Where did he go?
- What do you mean?

969
01:04:10,868 --> 01:04:12,008
You don't know where the patient is?

970
01:04:49,908 --> 01:04:51,178
I really found him.

971
01:04:55,078 --> 01:04:56,078
My father.

972
01:05:05,888 --> 01:05:07,328
Cha Hong Du.

973
01:05:07,398 --> 01:05:10,928
No, it doesn't matter what your real name is.

974
01:05:12,368 --> 01:05:13,638
But this is it.

975
01:05:15,938 --> 01:05:17,738
The fake world you believe in...

976
01:05:19,038 --> 01:05:22,038
is the world I have to create for you.

977
01:05:31,648 --> 01:05:34,458
(Oh! My Guard)
